    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nAs in the title.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nStart with running the shell command\n\n```\nnvim --clean\n```\n\nInside Nvim runs:\n\n```\n:tnoremap <C-J>a <Cmd>wincmd w<CR>\n:auto TermLeave <buffer> echom \"leaving normal buffer\"\n:vsplit\n:term\n```\n\nAt this point, the terminal window is focused, but not in terminal-mode.  Run:\n\n```\n:auto TermLeave <buffer> echom \"leaving terminal buffer\"\n```\n\nEnter terminal-mode:\n\n```\ni\n```\n\nTrigger the mapping:\n\n```\nCtrl-J a\n```\n\nObserve `leaving normal buffer` instead of `leaving terminal buffer`.\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nObserve `leaving terminal buffer` instead.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.12.4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nterminal mode in vim and nvim are entirely different, not comparable\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nUbuntu 22\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\ngnome-terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nnot relevant\n\n### Installation\n\nsnap",
