            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> I don't think this is a bug.\n\nPossibly. What about providing a hook in the TermLeave autocmd to know which terminal is leaving the term mode?\n\n(Because all terminals' normal mode state are \"shared\", maybe the correct answer is simply \"all terminals in all windows\"? In this case... I guess all you need is a brief comment in the documentation explaining the situation.)\n\nMotivation: I want to show relativenumber in terminals that are focused and in normal mode (i.e. more or less vim's terminal behavior if relativenumber is set), but not otherwise. My current code is\n\n<details><summary>code (long)</summary>\n\n```vim\nhighlight Ignore ctermfg=0 guifg=bg  \" github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41096\n\nfunction s:HideRelativeNumber()\n\tsetl rnu winhighlight+=LineNr:Ignore,LineNrAbove:Ignore,LineNrBelow:Ignore\nendfunction\n\nfunction s:ShowRelativeNumber()\n\tsetl rnu winhighlight-=LineNr:Ignore,LineNrAbove:Ignore,LineNrBelow:Ignore\nendfunction\n\nfunction s:OnTermEnter()\n\tcall s:HideRelativeNumber()\nendfunction\n\nfunction s:OnTermLeave()\n\tif &buftype == \"terminal\"\n\t\tcall s:ShowRelativeNumber()\n\tendif\nendfunction\n\nfunction s:OnWinEnter()\n\tif &buftype == \"terminal\"\n\t\tif exists('w:should_startinsert_when_enter')\n\t\t\tunlet w:should_startinsert_when_enter\n\t\t\tstartinsert\n\t\tendif\n\t\tif mode()==#'t'\n\t\t\tcall s:HideRelativeNumber()\n\t\telse\n\t\t\tcall s:ShowRelativeNumber()\n\t\tendif\n\tendif\nendfunction\n\nfunction s:OnWinLeave()\n\tif &buftype == \"terminal\"\n\t\tif mode()==#'t'\n\t\t\tlet w:should_startinsert_when_enter=1\n\t\tendif\n\t\tcall s:HideRelativeNumber()\n\tendif\nendfunction\n\naugroup termrelno\n\tauto!\n\tauto TermEnter * call s:OnTermEnter()\n\tauto TermLeave * call s:OnTermLeave()\n\tauto WinEnter * call s:OnWinEnter()\n\tauto WinLeave * call s:OnWinLeave()\naugroup END\n```\n</details>\n\nHonestly seem pretty clunky. Why can't I just do this?\n\n``` vim\naugroup termrelno\n\tauto!\n\tauto TermEnter * call s:HideRelativeNumber()\n\tauto TermLeave * call s:ShowRelativeNumber()\naugroup END\n```",
